      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has a room-temperature compressive yield strength of 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has limited room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo provides strong solid-solution strengthening and contributes to high room-temperature strength.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo content produces a high electronegativity difference in the baseline alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-associated electronegativity difference reduces ductility.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A fraction of Mo should be replaced with Nb, lowering the Mo/Nb ratio.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Mo with Nb will reduce the alloy's overall electronegativity difference.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing Mo with Nb will modify lattice distortion in the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced electron-density mismatch will lessen dislocation pinning and ease dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After partial Mo-to-Nb substitution, solid-solution strengthening will remain sufficient to preserve high strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial Mo-to-Nb substitution will increase room-temperature compressive plastic strain before failure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain a compressive yield strength close to 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A limited range of Mo-to-Nb substitution can preserve the disordered BCC structure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive reduction of Mo may cause a significant loss of strength.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using identical processing conditions, such as spark plasma sintering, will ensure maintenance of the BCC phase across the alloy series.",
